From: EC2 Default User <ec2-user@ip-172-31-7-30.us-east-2.compute.internal>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:29:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: repair FP4 x block-sparse composition on SM100

- vendor era-matched (8fecc234) SM100 block-sparse helpers as
  block_sparse_utils_fp4.py and point flash_fwd_sm100_fp4.py at them;
  the shared block_sparse_utils.py moved to a pipeline-object protocol
  the FP4 kernel's mbar-offset call sites were never migrated to
- interface: pass q_stage (2 on SM100) instead of compute_capability to
  get_block_sparse_expected_shapes
- interface: fill the dense SM100 kernel's descale_tensors positional slot
- interface: re-pack runtime block-sparse args to the 8-field structure
  the compiled signature was traced with
- unpack only the first 4 fields of BlockSparseTensors in the vendored
  helpers (NamedTuple gained trailing fields)

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
